    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0241",
      "sequence": 253,
      "meaning": "The royal youths arrive at that moment, their bodies clothed in loveliness. The accomplished, heroic oceans of virtue—one dark, one fair—shine in the royal assembly like two full moons among the stars. Each person sees the Lord according to the disposition of the heart: great warriors behold embodied heroic ardour; crooked kings see a massive, terrifying form; demons hidden in royal guise see Death openly before them; townspeople see the two brothers as ornaments of humanity and a delight to the eyes. The women joyfully behold a supremely matchless figure of Beauty itself, each according to her own taste.",
