    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0242",
      "sequence": 254,
      "meaning": "Scholars see the Lord as the cosmic Person with countless faces, hands, feet, eyes and heads. Janaka’s people see the brothers as dear relatives; Janaka and his queens love them like children; yogis see the serene, pure, even, self-luminous supreme reality; and devotees of Hari see their chosen deity, giver of every joy. Sītā’s gaze upon Rāma carries a love and happiness that even she cannot express, much less any poet. Thus the Lord of Kosala appears to each according to that person’s inward feeling, while the dark and fair princes shine in the royal gathering and steal the eyes of the world.",
