    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0243",
      "sequence": 255,
      "meaning": "Both brothers possess an effortless beauty for which even millions of Loves are too small a comparison. Their lovely faces shame the autumn moon; lotus eyes delight the heart, and their graceful glances steal the mind. Fine cheeks, swaying earrings, chins, lips and gentle speech are beautiful; their smiles outshine the moon, and their arched brows and shapely noses enchant. Marks gleam on broad foreheads, while rows of bees would blush before their hair. Yellow head-cloths adorned here and there with flower buds grace their heads. Three fine conch-like lines cross their necks, as though marking the boundary of all three worlds’ beauty. Pearl necklets and tulasī garlands adorn their chests; with bull-like shoulders, lionlike bearing and vast arms, they are treasuries of strength.",
