    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0244",
      "sequence": 256,
      "meaning": "Yellow cloth is tied at their waists beside their quivers; they hold arrows and bows, with the splendid bow resting on the left shoulder. Yellow sacred threads shine upon them, and beauty covers them from toenail to crown. Everyone who sees them becomes happy and cannot turn away a fixed gaze. Janaka rejoices at the two brothers, goes to clasp the sage’s lotus feet, tells his story and shows him the whole arena. Wherever the excellent princes go, everyone looks on in wonder; each person sees Rāma according to a particular inclination, though no one knows his deeper mystery. The sage praises the fine arrangement, delighting the king, who seats him and the two brothers on the one clear, spacious and beautiful platform surpassing all the others.",
