    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0245",
      "sequence": 257,
      "meaning": "At sight of the Lord all the kings lose heart, as stars fade when the full moon rises. They become convinced that Rāma will break the bow and, even before it is broken, Sītā will place the garland upon his breast; some urge one another to return home rather than lose fame, majesty, strength and splendour. Other rulers—blind with pride and without discernment—laugh at this counsel: even if the bow is broken, they say, the wedding will be hard to accomplish, while without breaking it no prince can wed her. Even if Death himself comes, they will defeat him in battle for Sītā. Hearing this, the wise, righteous devotees of Hari smile: after Rāma has humbled the kings’ pride, who could defeat Daśaratha’s battle-seasoned sons and marry Sītā?",
